  "description": "Deleting with Condition (1)",
  "code": "DELETE FROM account\n     WHERE branch_name IN\n         (SELECT branch_name\n          FROM branch\n          WHERE branch_city = 'Brooklyn');",
  "line_count": 5,
  "has_explanations": true,
  "lines": [
    {
      "line_no": 1,
      "code": "DELETE FROM account",
      "explanation": "The target table 'account' is specified. "
    },
    {
      "line_no": 2,
      "code": "     WHERE branch_name IN",
      "explanation": "IN is set membership test. It tests whether a data value matches on of a list of target values. The IN in this line compares branch names with the subquery results that are branches in 'Brookly'."
    },
    {
      "line_no": 3,
      "code": "         (SELECT branch_name",
      "explanation": "In this example, the subquery to find branch located in 'Brooklyn' is used and by comparing the list of results, they choose the accounts opened in the branches."
    },
    {
      "line_no": 4,
      "code": "          FROM branch",
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "line_no": 5,
      "code": "          WHERE branch_city = 'Brooklyn');",
      "explanation": "WHERE clause is to choose certain rows of data by condition. 'WHERE' keyword is followed by the comparison and this example is to choose the rows which is located in 'Brookly' as the branch city and delete the information. 'branch_city' column has character domain type, so in order to compare the value, the test value should be character too. In addition, the test value 'Brookly' is embraced with single quotation, because it is character. "
    }
  ],
